Sval: Stop piling up OffscreenCanvas frames while the window is hidden

Backport of Mozilla's Bug 2068559 (mozilla-central 60fb197bead1,
Firefox 159). Only the context of the OffscreenCanvasDisplayHelper.h
member hunk is adapted, to ESR 153's member list; the logic is
unchanged. Mozilla landed no test for it.

While a window was minimized or occluded, its compositor was paused,
but a page drawing to an OffscreenCanvas kept presenting a frame each
time. Each frame held a remote texture the paused compositor never
consumed, so memory grew by gigabytes in seconds until the window was
shown again, on Linux, Windows and macOS alike. The canvas element
now observes its document's activity and tells the display helper
whether its browsing context is active. While it is inactive, the
helper keeps the drawn content in the context's own buffers and
presents only the latest frame once the document is active again.

